.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH acc-check 1  "check 0.6.0" 
.SH NAME
acc\-check \- Enforce policy against a manifest, honoring recorded dispositions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacc check\fR [\fB\-\-policy\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-as\-of\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enforce policy against a manifest, honoring recorded dispositions
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Policy file; overrides the policy embedded in the manifest
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-as\-of\fR \fI<DATE>\fR
Calendar date dispositions are evaluated on (YYYY\-MM\-DD). Required when any finding has a non\-open disposition; the machine clock is never consulted
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra diagnostics on stderr (resolved policy, format, destination, counts). Never changes stdout
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format; inferred from the \-\-output extension when omitted
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
yaml
.IP \(bu 2
table: A plain\-text table for people; `text` is an alias
.IP \(bu 2
sarif
.IP \(bu 2
in\-toto: An unsigned in\-toto Statement v1 whose predicate is the manifest
.IP \(bu 2
in\-toto\-jsonl: JSON Lines of unsigned in\-toto Statements, one per change
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never color diagnostics. acc\*(Aqs own output is never colored; this and a non\-empty NO_COLOR environment variable switch off color in help and usage errors too
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
A manifest (JSON or YAML) written by `scan` or `evaluate`
.SH VERSION
v0.6.0
